WEBVTT


00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:07.440
Placing markers as we're knitting can
be a real help to keep track of things

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.560
as we're knitting along when you're
seaming long pieces or the side seams

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.720
of sweaters, for example, it's helpful
to have markers at regular intervals on

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.150
both the front and the back side seams.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:26.200
This can make it a lot easier
to precisely join the seam.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.129
The most common use of markers is
when knitting a drop shoulder sweater.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.500
It's really helpful to have a marker
at the start of the armhole opening.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.790
So when it comes time to join
the sleeves, you'll know exactly

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.349
where they should be positioned.

00:00:44.769 --> 00:00:50.140
You use DesignaKnit, Original Pattern
Drafting and add markers as you create

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:55.000
your garment pieces, and the markers
will be included in some of the outputs.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:01:02.385
Interactive knitting, garment outline and
garment notation formats include markers.

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:06.835
Let's practice this in
Standard Garment Syling.

00:01:06.855 --> 00:01:10.965
We'll create a simple drop shoulder
or a straight sleeve style.

00:01:12.435 --> 00:01:15.105
I'll just go through and
accept all the defaults.

00:01:15.105 --> 00:01:17.655
We want to get some pieces on the screen.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.360
Then switched to Original Pattern Drafting
and we'll start playing with markers.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.840
Select the front piece and zoom in.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.560
There are two ways to set markers.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.030
You can use the menu item,
>technique, >set marker.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:37.740
Look!

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.570
DesignaKnit is smart enough to recognize
this as a drop shoulder sweater and

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:47.775
it automatically places markers at the
underarm points where we want them.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:53.775
Now another way to turn on
markers is to use the marker tool.

00:01:54.585 --> 00:01:58.425
You can use either one of these
methods to turn the display on and

00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:02.835
off, but once the marker is set,
you don't have to display them.

00:02:02.985 --> 00:02:04.065
They'll be remembered.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.030
Let's add a marker halfway through
the side seam of our front.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:15.090
If you turn on the marker tool and click
and click and click, nothing happens.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.000
Markers are assigned to points.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.380
Use the plus or the add tool.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.390
Since I have mirroring on
appoint will be positioned on

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.250
each side of the front piece.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.485
I can now turn a marker
on those two points.

00:02:35.325 --> 00:02:39.315
To use these points with printable
instructions, click >file and

00:02:39.315 --> 00:02:43.005
>print, choose garment outline.

00:02:44.265 --> 00:02:49.095
Then click the single wrench button
and make sure that the checkbox

00:02:49.125 --> 00:02:51.405
"include markers" is checked.

00:02:52.515 --> 00:02:57.525
When you print or preview the
outline, the markers will be included.

00:02:58.035 --> 00:03:00.705
This is helpful if you
use these for blocking.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.760
Let's look at garment notation.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:13.970
Choose garment notation, click on
that single wrench and click the

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.220
"include markers" check box again.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:23.120
This time when you print or preview the
row numbers of the markers are included

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.670
with the Japanese notation instructions.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.810
Finally, when using interactive knitting.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:33.329
You'll be alerted when to place markers.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.710
set marker.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.120
Please take time to learn
this really helpful feature of

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.340
DesignaKnit and Happy Knitting!.

